WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.800
hello in this video i will be going over

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.400
the main patterns you will find in the

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.680
game of minesweeper

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.320
and how they work being aware of the

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.519
recurring patterns

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:10.960
will stop you having to work out the

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.799
same logic multiple times

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:14.639
and will make solving the game quicker

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.400
and easier

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.240
in my opinion these are the main

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.000
patterns in the game that are useful to

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.680
start off learning

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.119
if you have come from my beginner's

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:25.199
guide video feel free to skip to the

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:26.880
timestamp of the ones that i have not

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.800
already explained

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.320
if you are just looking for answers to

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.159
all of these there is an imgur link in

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:34.239
the description for you

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:35.920
let's start with the three on the

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.280
straight

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.520
probably the most basic one that i would

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.040
even call a pattern

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.360
but since on a straight line like this

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.760
it can only be next to three cells

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.000
so you can always flag along the line

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:52.559
the one one and the two one are the two

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:53.920
fundamental patterns

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.879
so let's move on to those next for the

00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:59.359
one one since the first two cells are

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.960
shared by both of the ones

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.960
the mind for the first one will always

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.479
satisfy the second one

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:07.680
so the third cell must always be free

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.320
note how this only works if there are no

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.280
other options

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.960
to the side of the first one

00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:18.479
the two one pattern is fairly similar

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:21.439
for the two this one tells us that there

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:21.920
is one

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.479
mine in these two cells which only

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:26.960
leaves one space for the second mine

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.000
so you can always flag here because the

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.240
other mine must be in these two

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.920
this cell also has to be free

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.400
these last two are quite commonly found

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.000
but often don't progress too much on

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.720
their own

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.399
which is where it's useful to extend

00:01:42.399 --> 00:01:45.600
them into the other patterns

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.840
the one two one is the most useful

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.200
pattern to look out for

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.840
and will quickly become your favorite

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.000
the only way to have two mines here

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.240
without putting two next to one of the

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.200
ones

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.439
is to have the mines on either side like

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:01.680
this

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.360
one two two one is another useful one

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.040
although seen less often than the one

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.959
two one in a way

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.520
this is a bit like two two one patterns

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.200
back to back

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.680
with the ones we know that there is only

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.680
one in these two cells

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.400
and one in these two cells so to

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.680
complete the twos

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.480
and not over satisfy the ones the flags

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.280
must be here

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.080
and here you can see how instead of

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.599
having to work out these two basic

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:31.440
patterns and put them together

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.680
knowing this pattern as its own thing

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.519
creates another shortcut to make things

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.519
easier

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:40.400
for the 1-1-1 pattern the mine must be

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.760
in the middle to satisfy

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.640
all of these ones if it was at either

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.120
edge

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.040
the one at the other side would not be

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.959
able to have a mine without putting two

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:51.440
minds next to the middle one

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.160
as an extension of the one one pattern

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:54.879
this again

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:56.959
doesn't apply when there are available

00:02:56.959 --> 00:03:00.319
cells to the sides

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.680
as for the one one one one pattern

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.400
the only way to satisfy all of the ones

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.040
here

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.560
is if the mines are at both of the ends

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.000
again basically two one one patterns

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.760
so the role of having no more

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.360
constraints to the sides

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.159
still applies

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:23.040
i hope that you found this helpful if

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.879
any of these weren't clear to you

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:26.959
it can be useful to go back and see why

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:28.640
each one worked

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.879
i find trying out the other variations

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:32.000
and seeing why they don't

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.920
work can help clear things up

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.920
thanks for watching if you haven't

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.400
already do check out my larger guide

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.640
i do go on to expand on how you can use

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.799
these patterns more effectively

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:47.840
go watch that right now or go play

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.080
minesweeper on mysuper.online

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.480
or follow me on twitch at twitchtv.com

